{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Perq Supervisor — Pre-Push Quality Gate (v4)",
  "version": "4.0.0",
  "description": "Blocks `git push` until ALL quality gates pass. Gate 0 requires every new user-facing function (window.X = function) to have a corresponding feature spec. Gate 4 is split into 4A (cache & asset integrity) and 4B (test coverage). v4 adds Gate 4B.7 (assertion density) and a mandatory SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED output block whenever a new feature spec is in the diff. A cache bump alone does NOT satisfy 4B. Both 4A and 4B must pass independently. This hook is the ONLY authority that blocks a push.",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": ["shell"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "PERQ SUPERVISOR HOOK v4 — pre-push quality gate.\n\nInspect the shell command about to run.\n\n## Step 1 — detect intent\n\nIf the command does NOT contain `git push` (case-insensitive substring), respond with exactly:\n\n  APPROVE: not a push, no gates required\n\nand do nothing else. Do not run gates.\n\nIf the command contains `git push`, run the full gate sequence below.\n\n## Step 2 — gate sequence\n\nExecute every gate. Do NOT short-circuit on a single failure — run all of them so the user sees the complete picture, then deny if any failed. Capture each result.\n\n### Gate 0 — Spec exists for new features\n\nRun: `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --name-only | grep -E 'preview-app\\.js'`\n\nIf `preview-app.js` is NOT in the diff: mark Gate 0 N/A and pass it.\n\nIf it IS in the diff, find every newly added user-facing global:\n  `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD -- preview-app.js | grep -E '^\\+.*window\\.[a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*\\s*=\\s*function'`\n\nFor EACH new `window.NAME = function`, the change is 'covered by a spec' iff EITHER:\n  (a) Some `.kiro/specs/*.md` contains the literal token `NAME` in § 1 'Problem Statement' or § 3 'Acceptance Criteria', OR\n  (b) Some `.kiro/specs/*.md` references `NAME` anywhere in its content AND the filename clearly identifies the feature (e.g., `feature-deal-detail-modal.md` covers `viewWalletDeal`).\n\nMechanical: `grep -lE \"\\\\b${NAME}\\\\b\" .kiro/specs/*.md` must return at least one path.\n\nIf any new function has no matching spec: FAIL — `DENY: gate 0 — [fn1, fn2] has no feature spec in .kiro/specs/`.\n\n'N/A (no spec)' is NEVER valid Gate 0 when new functions exist. The author must write a spec at `.kiro/specs/feature-<slug>.md` BEFORE pushing.\n\n### Gate 1 — JS syntax\n`node --check preview-app.js` must exit 0.\n\n### Gate 2 — Node script test suite\n`npm test` must exit 0 with zero FAILs across all sub-suites (gamif, load, migration, render, brand, splash). Capture per-suite PASS counts for the SUMMARY line.\n\n### Gate 3 — Playwright smoke\n`npm run test:smoke` must exit 0 with all tests passed.\n\n### Gate 4A — Cache & Asset Integrity\n\n**4A.1 — Cache buster.** If `preview-app.js` is in the diff, `preview.html` must be too AND its `?v=N` must have advanced. Compare current `preview.html` ?v= against `git show HEAD~1:preview.html | grep -oE 'preview-app\\.js\\?v=[0-9]+'`.\n\n**4A.2 — Service worker version.** If a SW exists at `service-worker.js`, `sw.js`, or `*.sw.js` in repo root or `dist/` AND any non-`preview-app.js` file changed, the SW's `CACHE_NAME` or `VERSION` must be bumped. If no SW in repo: N/A.\n\n**4A.3 — No orphan asset references.** Scan `preview.html` for `src=\"<file>\"` and `href=\"<file>\"` (excluding `http(s)://`, `data:`, `mailto:`, `tel:`, `sms:`, `#anchor`, `${}` template fragments). Each relative path must exist on disk. Any missing → fail with the path.\n\n### Gate 4B — Test Coverage\n\n**4B.1 — New functions have tests.** For each new `window.NAME = function` from Gate 0's list, confirm `NAME` appears in some `scripts/perq-*-test.js` or `tests/perq-smoke.spec.js`. Any new global without a test reference is a fail.\n\n**4B.2 — Edge case categories + SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED block.**\n\nIf a NEW feature spec was added (`git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --name-only | grep '^\\.kiro/specs/'` is non-empty), do BOTH of the following:\n\nFirst — verify edge case categories. The feature's tests must collectively cover the edge cases that apply: invalid/null input, network failure (only if the feature touches fetch/XHR), offline state (only if the feature uses online-dependent APIs), permission denied (only if the feature uses Camera/Geolocation/Notifications). Inspect § 5 'Edge cases + error states' of the spec for the declared cases. For each declared case, confirm at least one test references it (by keyword in test name, comment, or assertion). If any declared case has no test, fail.\n\nSecond — emit the SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED block. This is MANDATORY OUTPUT on EVERY push that includes a new spec. It does not block the push but it MUST appear in the output. Format exactly:\n\n  SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED:\n  Edge case: <name from spec § 5> → Test: <test file path or test name> → Assertion: <exact line of assertion code>\n  Edge case: <name from spec § 5> → Test: <test file path or test name> → Assertion: <exact line of assertion code>\n  ...\n\nList ONE row per declared edge case from § 5. If a case has no covering test, write `Test: NOT COVERED → Assertion: —` for that row (this also counts as a 4B.2 failure). Pull the exact assertion line by greping the relevant test file for the case keyword and showing the matching `if (...) pass++` or `assert.X` line verbatim.\n\nThis block is the human's one required touchpoint per feature. The hook does not validate the human's review, but the block must be present.\n\nIf no spec was added in this commit, mark 4B.2 N/A and skip the SPOT-CHECK block.\n\n**4B.3 — New tests wired into both pipelines.** If a new `scripts/perq-*-test.js` was added, confirm it appears in BOTH `package.json` `\"test\"` script AND `.github/workflows/android-build.yml` (or `docs/ci-workflow/android-build.yml`). Missing from either → fail.\n\n**4B.4 — Smoke spec ran against current code.** Mirrors Gate 3.\n\n**4B.5 — Coverage floor on critical path.** Heuristic: every TOP-LEVEL function added in `preview-app.js` must be referenced by name in at least one test file. Find new top-level functions with `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD -- preview-app.js | grep -E '^\\+(window\\.|function )([a-zA-Z_$][a-zA-Z0-9_$]*)'`. If <80% of new functions are referenced in `scripts/perq-*.js` or `tests/`, fail. If 0 new functions, N/A.\n\n**4B.6 — TEST_RESULTS.md current.** Either `TEST_RESULTS.md` is in the diff OR its first 5 lines contain today's UTC date (`YYYY-MM-DD`). Otherwise fail with 'TEST_RESULTS.md not refreshed for this push'.\n\n**4B.7 — No empty or trivial tests (NEW in v4).**\n\nFor every NEW test case added to `scripts/perq-*-test.js` in this commit, the case must contain at least ONE real assertion. \n\nMechanical procedure:\n\n  1. Run `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD -- scripts/perq-*-test.js` and isolate added (`^+`) lines, excluding `^+++` headers.\n  2. Identify 'test cases' as contiguous added blocks that contain `pass++`, `fail++`, or `it(`/`test(`/`describe(` markers.\n  3. For each such block, look for any of these assertion patterns inside its added lines:\n     - `assert.`, `assertEqual`, `assertStrictEqual`, `expect(`\n     - `throws(`, `rejects(`, `toThrow(`\n     - Comparison operators applied to a value: `===`, `!==`, `>=`, `<=`, `>`, `<`\n     - String/array predicates on a return value: `.includes(`, `.match(`, `.contains(`, `.toBe(`, `.toEqual(`, `.toHaveText(`, `.toHaveAttribute(`, `.toBeVisible(`, `.toBeHidden(`, `.toBeDefined(`\n  4. A test case lacking ALL of the above is 'trivial' and fails 4B.7.\n  5. The 'test name' for the deny line is the closest preceding `console.error('...')`, code comment, or `it/test/describe('NAME', ...)` invocation. If none, use `<file>:<line-number>`.\n\nFailure form: `DENY: gate 4B.7 — [<testName1>, <testName2>] has no assertions`.\n\nIf no test files were modified in this commit, mark 4B.7 N/A. If every new test case has at least one assertion, PASS.\n\n### Gate 5 — CHANGELOG\n\n`docs/CHANGELOG.md` must be in the diff OR commit subject must begin with `chore:`, `docs:`, `test:`, or `ci:` (these scopes are exempt). `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `perf:`, `style:` require a CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## Step 3 — respond\n\nProduce a markdown table with EVERY gate's status. Format (Gate 0 first; 15 rows total in v4):\n\n| Gate | Status | Evidence |\n|------|--------|----------|\n| 0. spec exists for new features | PASS/FAIL/N-A | list of new fns + spec file matched |\n| 1. node --check preview-app.js | PASS/FAIL | exit code |\n| 2. npm test | PASS/FAIL | per-suite PASS count |\n| 3. npm run test:smoke | PASS/FAIL | N/M passed |\n| 4A.1 cache buster | PASS/FAIL/N-A | v=N → v=M, or 'preview-app.js unchanged' |\n| 4A.2 service worker | PASS/FAIL/N-A | file path or 'no SW in repo' |\n| 4A.3 orphan assets | PASS/FAIL | count of missing files |\n| 4B.1 new fns tested | PASS/FAIL/N-A | list of new fns + test references |\n| 4B.2 edge cases | PASS/FAIL/N-A | spec path + cases checked |\n| 4B.3 tests wired | PASS/FAIL/N-A | new test file + 'in npm test' + 'in CI' |\n| 4B.4 smoke ran | PASS/FAIL | mirrors gate 3 |\n| 4B.5 coverage floor | PASS/FAIL/N-A | X/Y functions referenced (Z%) |\n| 4B.6 TEST_RESULTS date | PASS/FAIL | last modified or date in file |\n| 4B.7 assertion density | PASS/FAIL/N-A | X new tests, Y with assertions (Z%) |\n| 5. CHANGELOG | PASS/FAIL/EXEMPT | scope + path |\n\nIf 4B.2 is not N/A (i.e., a new spec was added), the table MUST be followed by the SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED block defined under 4B.2. The block is mandatory output. Push is not blocked by it but the table is incomplete without it.\n\nThen the SUMMARY line:\n\nSUMMARY: <prev-total> → <new-total> test cases, +<delta> <feature-tag>\n\nThen the verdict:\n- All applicable sub-gates pass: `APPROVE: all gates passed`\n- Any sub-gate fails: `DENY: gate <X.Y> — <one-line reason with the bash line that proves it>`\n\nDo NOT short-circuit. Do NOT silently skip. Do NOT mark a sub-gate N/A unless its precondition genuinely doesn't apply. Gate 0 has the strictest rule — if `preview-app.js` adds a `window.X = function`, Gate 0 cannot be N/A.\n\n## Notes\n\n- This is the ONLY hook that BLOCKS a push. The agentStop companion (`perq-supervisor-report.kiro.hook`) reports but never denies.\n- Cache bump alone does NOT satisfy Gate 4B. 4A and 4B are independent.\n- Force-push, push-to-tag, branches other than `main` — all go through all gates.\n- If `npm install` is needed, run it first; count its exit status as part of Gate 2.\n- The steering file at `.kiro/steering/perq.md` is authoritative for project conventions; the gates above enforce mechanical correctness."
  }
}
